      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the timer module could be clearer on this, but AFAICT, enabled timers are ones where you previously set a timeout and haven\u0027t disabled them yet. Expired timers are enabled timers where the timeout has passed. Disabled timers are not expired. The expected usages is enable, then is_expired, then disable.\n\nI agree that there are too many timers to keep track of in this state. I\u0027m not sure what would be a good way to improve it without departing from the spec. I did create b:231326418 to make the TC responsible for waiting for VCONN to transition, and that would mean we wouldn\u0027t need this timer here.",
